    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice. i hear you on being empathetic, but at the end of the day, a business has to stay competitive and efficient to survive. it feels like there's a growing consensus that moving toward highly automated, lean teams is just the inevitable logical progression for any modern company. do you think there's any real legitimate argument for resisting this shift, or is it just a matter of how well a company manages the transition?",
